Generic local modifications (Myoxus contributors, 2026):

- PostgreSQL: attach an existing pool without running library migrations;
  filter registered definition hashes before the polling limit; admit a
  snapshot without rewinding a concurrent admission; participate in a caller's
  transaction for snapshot creation/restart and signal admission. Snapshot
  sidecar updates follow successful snapshot admission. Correlated events retain
  their consumed identity and advance the snapshot in the same transaction.
  A caller-supplied native wait arbiter runs before snapshot locks, using that
  transaction for absolute deadlines and already-committed acceptance. Existing
  pooled polling advances due/buffered waits using the current signal projection.
- Runtime: register definitions in a live shared index for the existing
  PooledWorker/external executor; expose worker completion and bounded shutdown
  with task reaping; respect zero retries and persist terminal exhausted
  external-task failures instead of leaving them executable. Polling and hints
  also admit checkpointed current tasks for claimed continuation, using retained
  output and existing completion helpers without calling the task executor again.
  Signal consumers preserve a backend's already-advanced checkpoint. External
  JSON branch selection retains its full input and technical routingKey; only
  the selected declared child chain participates in continuation/completion.
  An explicit routingEmpty projection completes an authored empty branch without
  dispatching a synthetic task; it cannot suppress a declared nonempty child.
  External dispatch resolves declared Branch selector names omitted by the
  upstream task index; native task dispatch keeps its indexed contract.
  Persisted advancement into another signal/delay head parks that control under
  the normal dispatch claim, sharing existing wait arbitration and event draining
  rather than invoking a nonexistent external task body.

Glirulus additionally changes package/library identities and sibling dependency
edges, preserves inherited tests, and carries standalone workspace packaging.
The upstream PostgreSQL integration test is verified against the recorded source
commit. Its omitted development dependencies are restored; all three disposable
container construction sites share an optional standalone-run cleanup label.

The original SQL object names and notification channel remain unchanged.
Application business types, authorization, native receipts, native wait
arbitration and application migration ledgers remain outside these libraries.

Additional Glirulus standalone-schema correction: migration
010_correlated_event_wait_projection.sql supplies nullable event_id,
accepted_at and consumed_at event columns, their partial unique admission key,
and the snapshot signal_name polling projection required by the generic source.
It is independently authored from the generic library SQL contracts under MIT,
Copyright (c) 2026 Daniel Scharf. The original nine upstream migrations remain
byte-for-byte unchanged. No application migration ledger, business constraints,
readiness marker or native tables are included; caller-managed pool attachment
continues to perform no DDL.

Additional Glirulus signal-store qualification corrections preserve inherited
FIFO consumption of uncorrelated buffered events when no matching wait or native
arbitrator applies. Correlated events retain their identities and native waits
retain arbitration before snapshot locks. Terminal signal completion flushes
its task output on the same connection before terminal state drops the task
map, preserving existing completion timestamps and avoiding unchanged-output
rewrites. The output, terminal snapshot and event consumption remain atomic;
no extra snapshot history checkpoint or independent transaction is introduced.
